# Backend API structure (`nwidart/laravel-modules`)

The API lives in `backend/`. Feature code uses **[nwidart/laravel-modules](https://nwidart.com/laravel-modules/v6/introduction)** (v12 for Laravel 12). Modules live under `backend/Modules/{Name}/` with namespace `Modules\{Name}\`.

Scaffold: `php artisan module:make {Name} --api`

## Platform vs modules

| Area | Path | Role |
|------|------|------|
| Platform | `app/Http/Middleware/`, `app/Providers/`, `app/Enums/`, `app/Support/`, `config/`, `database/` | Auth guards, middleware, shared config, cross-cutting helpers |
| Shell API | `app/Http/Controllers/` (e.g. health) + `routes/api.php` | Non-feature endpoints only; `routes/api.php` is a **thin registry** |
| Feature modules | `Modules/{Name}/` | Controllers, requests, models, services, module routes |

`{Name}` is **PascalCase**, singular, aligned with frontend modules when they exist (`Appointment` ↔ `src/modules/appointment`, `User` ↔ `src/modules/user`, `Auth` ↔ auth).

## Module folder layout

```
Modules/{Name}/
  app/
    Http/Controllers/
    Http/Requests/
    Http/Resources/       # optional
    Models/
    Services/             # business logic; no HTTP
    Providers/            # *ServiceProvider, RouteServiceProvider
  routes/
    api.php               # feature API routes (already under /api prefix)
    web.php               # leave empty unless needed
  database/               # optional module migrations/seeders
  module.json
  composer.json
```

Autoload: root `composer.json` merges `Modules/*/composer.json` via `wikimedia/composer-merge-plugin`. After adding modules: `composer dump-autoload`.

## Data flow (strict)

```
Modules/{Name}/routes/api.php  →  Controllers  →  Services  →  Models
                                      ↑
                               Http/Requests
```

- **Controllers** — HTTP only: authorize, validate (FormRequest), call services, return `JsonResponse`.
- **Services** — domain logic (meetings, stats). Injectable via constructor.
- **Models** — persistence + relationships + small helpers (`isCompleted()`, `canJoinMeeting()`).
- **Requests** — `authorize()` + `rules()`.

## Routing

- Module `RouteServiceProvider` loads `routes/api.php` with `middleware('api')->prefix('api')`.
- Do **not** add another `api` or `v1` prefix in module routes — keep paths like `/appointments`, `/users`, `/auth/...` so frontend URL maps stay valid.
- `backend/routes/api.php` registers only shell routes (e.g. `/health`).

## Existing modules

| Module | Owns |
|--------|------|
| `Auth` | login, register, me, logout |
| `User` | `User` model, admin CRUD, `UserResource` |
| `Appointment` | appointments, slots, ratings, meetings, availability, expertise, mentor profile, admin stats |

## Naming

| Item | Example |
|------|---------|
| Controller | `Modules\Appointment\Http\Controllers\AppointmentController` |
| Form request | `StoreAppointmentRequest` |
| Service | `AppointmentMeetingService`, `GoogleMeetService` |
| Model | `Modules\User\Models\User`, `Modules\Appointment\Models\Appointment` |

## JSON API shape

- Collections / entities: `['data' => ...]`
- Validation: Laravel / `ValidationException`
- Keep field shapes in sync with `src/modules/*/types/*.types.ts`

## When adding code

| What | Where |
|------|--------|
| New feature endpoint | `php artisan module:make {Name} --api` (or extend existing module) |
| Shared non-HTTP helper | `app/Support/` |
| Migration / app seeder | `database/` (or module `database/` when scoped) |
| Third-party integration | Module `app/Services/` |

## Do not

- Add feature controllers under `app/Http/Controllers/Api/`.
- Put feature Eloquent models in `app/Models/`.
- Embed heavy aggregation in controllers — use a service.
- Change API paths without updating frontend `services/*Service.ts` and types.
